course: dictionary
lesson: 9550
title: Measuring time with a stopwatch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stopwatch is a clock that you start and stop yourself, by pressing a button, to measure exactly how long something takes. «A stopwatch is a clock you start and stop to measure how long something takes, often to a tenth or hundredth of a second.» The words start and stop are the clue to what it does.
explain: Use the context to work out meanings. In «Think of a school sports day», each class cheers for its own team, but the stopwatch is the same for everyone, so it gives a fair way to time races. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: A stopwatch is a tool, like a ruler or scales. «We choose a tool that fits the job: a ruler or tape measure for length, scales for mass, a clock or stopwatch for time and a thermometer for temperature.» So when the job is measuring time, the stopwatch is the right tool.
fact: A stopwatch is a clock you start and stop to measure how long something takes.
fact: A stopwatch can measure time to a tenth or a hundredth of a second.
fact: In science, a stopwatch can time how long a ball takes to fall, or how long a pendulum takes to swing.
fact: In PE, a stopwatch times races.
fact: Reaction time, the delay between seeing something and pressing the button, can cause small errors in stopwatch times.
exercise: «A stopwatch is a clock you start and stop to measure how long something takes.» What is a stopwatch for? | To show the date | *To measure how long something takes | To weigh things
exercise: In science, Priya uses a stopwatch to time a ball as it falls. What is she measuring? | *Time | Length | Mass | Temperature
exercise: Which tool fits the job of timing a race? | Scales | *Stopwatch | Ruler | Thermometer
test: Why do PE teachers use a stopwatch at sports day? | To show the time of day | To make the race longer | To count the number of runners | *So every runner is timed in the same way
test: A stopwatch can measure to a hundredth of a second. What does a hundredth of a second mean? | *A very small part of one second | One minute | A hundred seconds | A hundred minutes
exam: Which tool is best for measuring how long a pendulum takes to swing? | Scales | Ruler | *Stopwatch | Thermometer
